  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <div class="container">
        <a href="/" class="back">← BACK</a>
        <h1>FAQ</h1>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="faq">
            <h2>IS IT FREE?</h2>
            <p>Yes. Completely free. No ads, no subscriptions, no catch. We built it because we needed it.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>DO I NEED TO DOWNLOAD ANYTHING?</h2>
            <p>Nope. It's a web app — just go to <a href="https://app.dirtylaundry.club">app.dirtylaundry.club</a> in your browser. You can add it to your home screen and it works like a native app. We're also working on an App Store version.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>HOW DO GROUPS WORK?</h2>
            <p>One person creates a group and shares an invite link. Everyone else taps the link and joins. That's it. You can have flatmates, partners, family — whoever shares your household.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>CAN KIDS USE IT?</h2>
            <p>Yes! Parents can set members as "kid" role. Kids can join without an email (just a name) and complete chores to earn points. They can't add chores or change settings — parents stay in control.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>HOW ARE POINTS CALCULATED?</h2>
            <p>Each chore has a point value set by whoever created it. Harder chores are worth more. You can boost chores with bounties to make them more tempting. The chore of the day is worth double.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>WHAT IF SOME PEOPLE ARE BUSIER THAN OTHERS?</h2>
            <p>The group owner can set a chore split — each person gets a percentage based on their availability. The reports score you against your share, not everyone else's. So someone with a 25% share who hits their target is doing just as well as someone with 50%.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>IS IT GOOD FOR ADHD?</h2>
            <p>We built it with ADHD in mind. The "Just Do One" mode shows you one chore at a time instead of an overwhelming list. Chore roulette takes the decision-making away. Points and reactions give you the dopamine hit your brain needs. And push notifications act as your external memory.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>IS MY DATA SAFE?</h2>
            <p>Your data is stored securely and only visible to your group members. We don't sell data, don't show ads, and don't use tracking. Read our full <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>CAN I USE IT ALONE?</h2>
            <p>You can, but it's designed for groups. The leaderboard, nudges, and reactions only make sense with other people. That said, the points and streaks work fine for solo motivation.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>HOW DO I GET STARTED?</h2>
            <p>Go to <a href="https://app.dirtylaundry.club/auth">app.dirtylaundry.club</a>, create an account, start a group, and pick a starter pack (student flat, family home, or couple). Takes about 60 seconds.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>HOW DO I DELETE MY ACCOUNT?</h2>
            <p>In the app, go to <strong>Profile → Delete Account</strong>. This permanently removes your profile, points, completions, and uploaded photos. If you'd prefer, email us and we'll handle it within 48 hours.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="faq">
            <h2>NEED HELP OR FOUND A BUG?</h2>
            <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@dirtylaundry.club">hello@dirtylaundry.club</a>. We're a small team and reply within a couple of days. For legal stuff, see our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>

